#: ../../operations.rst:894
msgid ""
"name                  via     issuer                                "
"expires              renews               state origin    ocsp error\n"
"*.example.org         dns-01  R11                                   "
"2027-02-22T10:00:00Z 2027-01-23T10:00:00Z ready listed    good -\n"
"example.org           http-01 R11                                   "
"2027-02-22T10:00:00Z 2027-01-23T10:00:00Z ready listed    good -\n"
"localhost             local   Sibuna_Local_Authority_-_Intermediate "
"2026-11-24T22:00:00Z 2026-11-24T18:00:00Z ready listed    -    -\n"
"shop.apps.example.org http-01 R11                                   "
"2027-02-22T10:00:00Z 2027-01-23T10:00:00Z ready on-demand good -\n"
"www.example.org       http-01 -                                     -     "
"               2026-11-24T10:04:00Z retry listed    -    VALIDATION "
"FAILED (ACME005)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:903
msgid ""
"``via`` says how the certificate is obtained: the challenge, or ``local`` "
"for the local authority. ``origin`` is ``listed`` for a name under "
"``auto`` and ``on-demand`` for a name that a handshake asked for. "
"``ocsp`` is ``good`` while a response is stapled, ``revoked`` when the "
"responder said so, and ``-`` otherwise. ``state`` is ``pending`` before "
"the first attempt, ``ordering`` during an order, ``waiting`` while "
"another node holds the lock, ``retry`` after a failure, and ``ready`` "
"otherwise. ``renews`` is the time of the next order. ``show stats`` and "
"the metrics endpoint add four series: "
"``sibuna_edge_acme_certificates_managed``, "
"``sibuna_edge_acme_certificates_served``, "
"``sibuna_edge_acme_nearest_expiry_seconds`` and "
"``sibuna_edge_acme_failures_total``. An alert on the third one tells us "
"when renewal has been failing for too long."
msgstr ""

